#%PAM-1.0
# Fingerprint-only PAM service — used exclusively by the Quickshell lockscreen's
# second PamContext (modules/lock/LockAuth.qml) to run a fingerprint scan in
# parallel with the normal password conversation ("passwd" service). Kept
# separate from system-auth on purpose: pam_fprintd has no timeout limit here
# (module restarts itself on failure — see LockAuth.qml), since this
# conversation isn't blocking anything else while it waits.
# max-tries=1: without it, pam_fprintd's own default (3) keeps this single
# conversation alive across up to 3 bad swipes before it ever calls
# completed() — LockAuth.qml's restart timer (which starts a brand new
# conversation, i.e. a fresh try counter) never gets a chance to run until
# all 3 are burned, so a wrong finger made a correct one afterwards feel
# stuck/slow. With max-tries=1, one bad swipe completes immediately and
# LockAuth.qml's own fast restart loop takes over instead.
auth       required     pam_fprintd.so max-tries=1
account    required     pam_permit.so
